\"name\":\"Greek Yogurt (plain, 0% fat)\",\"amount\":\"2 tbsp\",\"calories\":15},{\"name\":\"Celery, diced\",\"amount\":\"1/4 cup\",\"calories\":4},{\"name\":\"Red Onion, minced\",\"amount\":\"1 tbsp\",\"calories\":2},{\"name\":\"Lettuce Leaves (e.g., butter lettuce)\",\"amount\":\"4 large leaves\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Whole Grain Crackers\",\"amount\":\"4 crackers\",\"calories\":100}],\"totalCalories\":289,\"macros\":{\"protein\":37,\"carbs\":25,\"fat\":5},\"instructions\":[\"In a bowl, flake the drained tuna.\",\"Add Greek yogurt, diced celery, and minced red onion. Mix well. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\",\"Spoon tuna salad into lettuce leaves to create wraps. Serve with whole grain crackers.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Chicken & Tofu Phở (modified, without noodles)\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"A warm and comforting Vietnamese dish, modified to be lower in carbs and higher in protein by omitting traditional noodles.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Chicken Breast, shredded (cooked)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":165},{\"name\":\"Firm Tofu, cubed (baked or pan-fried)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":145},{\"name\":\"Phở Broth (homemade or low sodium)\",\"amount\":\"2 cups\",\"calories\":60},{\"name\":\"Bean Sprouts\",\"amount\":\"1 cup\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Bok Choy, chopped\",\"amount\":\"1 cup\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Fresh Basil & Cilantro\",\"amount\":\"1/4 cup\",\"calories\":2},{\"name\":\"Lime Wedge\",\"amount\":\"1\",\"calories\":2},{\"name\":\"Jalapeño slices (optional)\",\"amount\":\"2-3 slices\",\"calories\":1}],\"totalCalories\":415,\"macros\":{\"protein\":46,\"carbs\":24,\"fat\":15},\"instructions\":[\"Heat phở broth until simmering. (For homemade, simmer chicken bones/carcass with ginger, onion, star anise, cinnamon for hours).\",\"In a large bowl, arrange shredded chicken, baked tofu, bean sprouts, and bok choy.\",\"Pour hot broth over the ingredients.\",\"Garnish with fresh basil, cilantro, a lime wedge, and jalapeño slices (if desired).\"]},\"snack\":{\"name\":\"Cottage Cheese with Sliced Cucumber\",\"time\":\"3:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A simple, high-protein snack for satiety.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Low-fat Cottage Cheese\",\"amount\":\"1 cup (220g)\",\"calories\":160},{\"name\":\"Cucumber, sliced\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":8}],\"totalCalories\":168,\"macros\":{\"protein\":28,\"carbs\":9,\"fat\":2},\"instructions\":[\"Serve cottage cheese in a bowl with sliced cucumber.\"]}},\"dailyTotals\":{\"calories\":1257,\"protein\":137,\"carbs\":95,\"fat\":37}},{\"dayNumber\":4,\"date\":\"Day 4\",\"meals\":{\"breakfast\":{\"name\":\"Whole Wheat Protein Pancakes with Berries\",\"time\":\"7:00 AM\",\"description\":\"A delicious and satisfying breakfast that\'s high in protein and fiber.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Whole Wheat Flour\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":200},{\"name\":\"Whey Protein Powder (unflavored or vanilla)\",\"amount\":\"1 scoop (30g)\",\"calories\":120},{\"name\":\"Egg White\",\"amount\":\"1 large\",\"calories\":17},{\"name\":\"Baking Powder\",\"amount\":\"1 tsp\",\"calories\":2},{\"name\":\"Unsweetened Almond Milk\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":15},{\"name\":\"Mixed Berries\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":40},{\"name\":\"Sugar-free Maple Syrup (optional)\",\"amount\":\"2 tbsp\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Cooking Spray\",\"amount\":\"as needed\",\"calories\":0}],\"totalCalories\":404,\"macros\":{\"protein\":31,\"carbs\":57,\"fat\":5},\"instructions\":[\"In a bowl, whisk together whole wheat flour, protein powder, baking powder.\",\"Add egg white and almond milk, mixing until just combined (do not overmix, lumps are okay).\",\"Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat, lightly spray with cooking spray.\",\"Pour 1/4 cup of batter per pancake. Cook for 2-3 minutes per side until golden brown.\",\"Serve pancakes topped with mixed berries and a drizzle of sugar-free maple syrup if desired.\"]},\"lunch\":{\"name\":\"Shrimp & Veggie Skewers with Brown Rice\",\"time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A light and lean meal with plenty of protein and colorful vegetables.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Shrimp (peeled, raw)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":140},{\"name\":\"Bell Pepper, chunks\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":15},{\"name\":\"Zucchini, chunks\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Cherry Tomatoes\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":14},{\"name\":\"Red Onion, chunks\",\"amount\":\"1/4 cup\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Olive Oil\",\"amount\":\"1 tsp\",\"calories\":40},{\"name\":\"Garlic Powder\",\"amount\":\"1/2 tsp\",\"calories\":5},{\"name\":\"Cooked Brown Rice\",\"amount\":\"1 cup\",\"calories\":215}],\"totalCalories\":447,\"macros\":{\"protein\":34,\"carbs\":50,\"fat\":11},\"instructions\":[\"Preheat grill or oven broiler. Thread shrimp and vegetables onto skewers.\",\"Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle with garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\",\"Grill or broil for 3-5 minutes per side, until shrimp are pink and cooked through and vegetables are tender-crisp.\",\"Serve skewers alongside cooked brown rice.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Tofu & Green Bean Curry (Vietnamese style)\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"A plant-based, flavorful curry rich in protein and fiber, with a creamy texture.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Firm Tofu, pressed & cubed\",\"amount\":\"200g\",\"calories\":290},{\"name\":\"Green Beans, trimmed\",\"amount\":\"1.5 cups\",\"calories\":50},{\"name\":\"Light Coconut Milk\",\"amount\":\"1/2 cup\",\"calories\":80},{\"name\":\"Red Curry Paste\",\"amount\":\"1 tbsp\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Onion, chopped\",\"amount\":\"1/2 medium\",\"calories\":20},{\"name\":\"Garlic, minced\",\"amount\":\"2 cloves\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Ginger, grated\",\"amount\":\"1 tbsp\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Fish Sauce (optional, for flavor)\",\"amount\":\"1 tsp\",\"calories\":3},{\"name\":\"Brown Rice\",\"amount\":\"1 cup (cooked)\",\"calories\":215}],\"totalCalories\":