\",\"calories\":248},{\"name\":\"Brown Rice, cooked\",\"amount\":\"180g (approx. 3/4 cup)\",\"calories\":200},{\"name\":\"Mixed Vegetables (broccoli, bell peppers, carrots)\",\"amount\":\"200g\",\"calories\":70},{\"name\":\"Soy Sauce (low sodium)\",\"amount\":\"1 tbsp\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Sesame Oil\",\"amount\":\"1 tsp\",\"calories\":40},{\"name\":\"Garlic & Ginger\",\"amount\":\"to taste\",\"calories\":10}],\"totalCalories\":576,\"macros\":{\"protein\":46,\"carbs\":53,\"fat\":17},\"instructions\":[\"Slice chicken breast into strips. Chop all vegetables.\",\"Heat sesame oil in a large pan or wok over medium-high heat. Add minced garlic and grated ginger, sauté for 30 seconds.\",\"Add chicken strips and stir-fry until cooked through.\",\"Add harder vegetables (carrots, broccoli) first, stir-fry for 3-4 minutes, then add bell peppers and stir-fry for another 2-3 minutes until tender-crisp.\",\"Stir in low-sodium soy sauce. Serve immediately over brown rice.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Baked Salmon with Quinoa & Roasted Asparagus\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"Omega-3 rich salmon paired with protein-packed quinoa and fiber-rich roasted asparagus.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Salmon Fillet\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":300},{\"name\":\"Quinoa, cooked\",\"amount\":\"180g (approx. 3/4 cup)\",\"calories\":218},{\"name\":\"Asparagus\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Olive Oil\",\"amount\":\"1 tbsp\",\"calories\":120},{\"name\":\"Lemon Wedge\",\"amount\":\"1\",\"calories\":5}],\"totalCalories\":673,\"macros\":{\"protein\":37,\"carbs\":44,\"fat\":37},\"instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 200°C (400°F).\",\"Season salmon with salt, pepper, and a squeeze of lemon juice. Toss asparagus with 1 tbsp olive oil, salt, and pepper.\",\"Place salmon and asparagus on a baking sheet. Bake for 12-15 minutes, or until salmon is cooked through and flakes easily.\",\"Serve salmon and asparagus with cooked quinoa.\"]},\"snack\":{\"name\":\"Protein Shake\",\"