, cucumber, cherry tomatoes, and bell pepper.\",\"Slice the grilled chicken and add to the salad. Add the cooked brown rice.\",\"Drizzle with olive oil and lemon juice. Toss gently and serve.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Pan-Seared Salmon with Roasted Sweet Potatoes & Asparagus\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"A delicious and nutrient-dense meal rich in omega-3s and fiber.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Salmon Fillet\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":300},{\"name\":\"Sweet Potato\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":130},{\"name\":\"Asparagus\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Olive Oil (for roasting)\",\"amount\":\"10ml\",\"calories\":90},{\"name\":\"Garlic (minced)\",\"amount\":\"5g\",\"calories\":7},{\"name\":\"Lemon Wedge\",\"amount\":\"1 unit\",\"calories\":2}],\"totalCalories\":559,\"macros\":{\"protein\":31,\"carbs\":36,\"fat\":33},\"instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 200°C (400°F).\",\"Peel and dice sweet potato. Toss with 5ml olive oil, salt, and pepper. Spread on a baking sheet and roast for 20-25 minutes, flipping halfway.\",\"Toss asparagus with remaining 5ml olive oil, minced garlic, salt, and pepper. Add to the baking sheet for the last 10-15 minutes of roasting.\",\"Pat salmon dry, season with salt and pepper. Heat a non-stick pan over medium-high heat. Add salmon skin-side down and sear for 4-5 minutes, then flip and cook for another 3-4 minutes, or until cooked to your liking.\",\"Serve salmon with roasted sweet potatoes and asparagus, garnished with a lemon wedge.\"]},\"snack\":{\"name\":\"Greek Yogurt with Honey & Walnuts\",\"time\":\"3:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A quick and satisfying snack rich in protein and healthy fats.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Greek Yogurt (plain, non-fat)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":90},{\"name\":\"Honey\",\"amount\":\"10g\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Walnuts\",\"amount\":\"20g\",\"calories\":130}],\"totalCalories\":250,\"macros\":{\"protein\":15,\"carbs\":25,\"fat\":15},\"instructions\":[\"Combine Greek yogurt with honey in a bowl.\",\"Top with chopped walnuts and enjoy.\"]}},\"dailyTotals\":{\"calories\":1796,\"protein\":125,\"carbs\":149,\"fat\":78}},{\"dayNumber\":2,\"date\":\"Day 2\",\"meals\":{\"breakfast\":{\"name\":\"Scrambled Eggs with Whole-Wheat Toast & Avocado\",\"time\":\"7:00 AM\",\"description\":\"A classic breakfast providing protein, healthy fats, and fiber.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Eggs (large)\",\"amount\":\"3 units\",\"calories\":210},{\"name\":\"Whole-Wheat Bread\",\"amount\":\"2 slices\",\"calories\":160},{\"name\":\"Avocado\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":80},{\"name\":\"Spinach\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Splash of Milk (for eggs)\",\"amount\":\"20ml\",\"calories\":10}],\"totalCalories\":470,\"macros\":{\"protein\":23,\"carbs\":38,\"fat\":25},\"instructions\":[\"Whisk eggs with a splash of milk, salt, and pepper.\",\"Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat. Add spinach and cook until wilted. Pour in egg mixture and scramble until cooked through.\",\"Toast the whole-wheat bread.\",\"Mash avocado and spread on toast. Serve scrambled eggs alongside.\"]},\"lunch\":{\"name\":\"Vietnamese Fresh Spring Rolls (Gỏi Cuốn) with Shrimp & Tofu\",\"time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"description\":\"Light and refreshing Vietnamese spring rolls, packed with protein and vegetables.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Rice Paper Wraps\",\"amount\":\"4 sheets\",\"calories\":100},{\"name\":\"Cooked Shrimp\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":100},{\"name\":\"Firm Tofu (pan-fried)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":140},{\"name\":\"Vermicelli Noodles (cooked)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":60},{\"name\":\"Lettuce Leaves\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Cucumber (julienned)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Fresh Herbs (mint, basil)\",\"amount\":\"20g\",\"calories\":5},{\"name\":\"Peanut Sauce (light, homemade)\",\"amount\":\"30g\",\"calories\":100}],\"totalCalories\":521,\"macros\":{\"protein\":30,\"carbs\":55,\"fat\":20},\"instructions\":[\"Prepare all ingredients: cook shrimp, pan-fry tofu until golden, cook vermicelli noodles, wash and chop vegetables/herbs.\",\"Dip one rice paper wrap in warm water until soft. Lay flat on a clean surface.\",\"Arrange a few shrimp halves, tofu strips, a small handful of vermicelli, lettuce, cucumber, and herbs near one edge.\",\"Fold the sides of the wrapper over the filling, then roll tightly from the bottom up.\",\"Repeat for remaining wraps. Serve immediately with light peanut sauce.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Lean Beef Stir-fry with Brown Rice\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"A quick and flavorful stir-fry packed with protein and colorful vegetables.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Lean Beef Sirloin (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":270},{\"name\":\"Brown Rice (cooked)\",\"amount\":\"120g\",\"calories\":132},{\"name\":\"Broccoli Florets\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":35},{\"name\":\"Carrots (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":20},{\"name\":\"Bell Pepper (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":15},{\"name\":\"Soy Sauce (low sodium)\",\"amount\":\"15ml\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Ginger (grated)\",\"amount\":\"5g\",\"calories\":5},{\"name\":\"Garlic (minced)\",\"amount\":\"5g\",\"calories\":7},{\"name\":\"Sesame Oil\",\"amount\":\"5ml\",\"calories\":45}],\"totalCalories\":534,\"macros\":{\"protein\":43,\"carbs\":50,\"fat\":19},\"instructions\":[\"Heat sesame oil in a large wok or pan over high heat.\",\"Add sliced beef and stir-fry until browned. Remove beef and set aside.\",\"Add broccoli, carrots, and bell pepper to the wok. Stir-fry for 3-5 minutes until tender-crisp. Add ginger and garlic and stir-fry for 1 minute more.\",\"Return beef to the wok. Add low-sodium soy sauce and toss to combine.\",\"Serve immediately over cooked brown rice.\"]},\"snack\":{\"name\":\"Protein Shake with Banana\",\"time\":\"3:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A quick and easy post-workout or mid-afternoon protein boost.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Whey Protein Powder (chocolate/vanilla)\",\"amount\":\"30g\",\"calories\":120},{\"name\":\"Banana (medium)\",\"amount\":\"1 unit\",\"calories\":105},{\"name\":\"Almond Milk (unsweetened)\",\"amount\":\"250ml\",\"calories\":40}],\"totalCalories\":265,\"macros\":{\"protein\":24,\"carbs\":38,\"fat\":5},\"instructions\":[\"Combine protein powder, banana, and almond milk in a blender.\",\"Blend until smooth. Drink immediately.\"]}},\"dailyTotals\":{\"calories\":1790,\"protein\":120,\"carbs\":181,\"fat\":69}},{\"dayNumber\":3,\"date\":\"Day 3\",\"meals\":{\"breakfast\":{\"name\":\"Spinach & Berry Protein Smoothie\",\"time\":\"7:00 AM\",\"description\":\"A vibrant and nutrient-packed smoothie to kickstart your day.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Spinach\",\"amount\":\"1 cup (packed)\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Mixed Berries (frozen)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":50},{\"name\":\"Banana (small)\",\"amount\":\"1 unit\",\"calories\":90},{\"name\":\"Whey Protein Powder (vanilla)\",\"amount\":\"25g\",\"calories\":100},{\"name\":\"Almond Milk (unsweetened)\",\"amount\":\"250ml\",\"calories\":40},{\"name\":\"Chia Seeds\",\"amount\":\"1 tbsp (15g)\",\"calories\":75}],\"totalCalories\":365,\"macros\":{\"protein\":28,\"carbs\":50,\"fat\":10},\"instructions\":[\"Combine all ingredients in a blender.\",\"Blend until completely smooth. Add a little more almond milk if needed for desired consistency. Serve immediately.\"]},\"lunch\":{\"name\":\"Vietnamese Lemongrass Chicken Bowl (Bún Gà Nướng style)\",\"time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A flavorful and satisfying Vietnamese-inspired bowl with grilled chicken and fresh vegetables.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Chicken Thigh (skinless, grilled)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":270},{\"name\":\"Vermicelli Noodles (cooked)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":120},{\"name\":\"Lettuce (shredded)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Cucumber (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Carrots (shredded)\",\"amount\":\"30g\",\"calories\":12},{\"name\":\"Bean Sprouts\",\"amount\":\"30g\",\"calories\":5},{\"name\":\"Nuoc Cham (light, homemade)\",\"amount\":\"30ml\",\"calories\":20},{\"name\":\"Peanuts (crushed)\",\"amount\":\"10g\",\"calories\":60}],\"totalCalories\":503,\"macros\":{\"protein\":38,\"carbs\":50,\"fat\":19},\"instructions\":[\"Marinate chicken thigh with minced lemongrass, garlic, a touch of soy sauce, and a tiny bit of honey for at least 30 minutes. Grill or pan-fry until cooked through and slightly caramelized.\",\"Cook vermicelli noodles according to package instructions.\",\"Prepare Nuoc Cham: mix fish sauce, water, lime juice, a touch of sweetener, minced garlic, and chili.\",\"In a large bowl, layer shredded lettuce, cucumber, carrots, bean sprouts, and vermicelli noodles.\",\"Slice the grilled chicken and place on top. Drizzle with Nuoc Cham and sprinkle with crushed peanuts. Serve.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Tofu & Vegetable Curry with Brown Rice\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"A flavorful vegetarian curry, rich in plant-based protein and fiber.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Firm Tofu (extra firm, pressed & cubed)\",\"amount\":\"200g\",\"calories\":280},{\"name\":\"Brown Rice (cooked)\",\"amount\":\"120g\",\"calories\":132},{\"name\":\"Coconut Milk (light)\",\"amount\":\"100ml\",\"calories\":90},{\"name\":\"Curry Paste (red/green)\",\"amount\":\"15g\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Mixed Vegetables (broccoli, bell pepper, snap peas)\",\"amount\":\"200g\",\"calories\":60},{\"name\":\"Vegetable Broth\",\"amount\":\"100ml\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Soy Sauce (low sodium)\",\"amount\":\"10ml\",\"calories\":7}],\"totalCalories\":609,\"macros\":{\"protein\":27,\"carbs\":60,\"fat\":29},\"instructions\":[\"Heat a pan over medium heat. Add curry paste and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.\",\"Add light coconut milk and vegetable broth, bring to a simmer.\",\"Add cubed tofu and mixed vegetables. Cook until vegetables are tender-crisp and tofu is heated through (about 8-10 minutes).\",\"Stir in low-sodium soy sauce. Serve hot with cooked brown rice.\"]},\"snack\":{\"name\":\"Apple Slices with Peanut Butter\",\"time\":\"3:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A classic and satisfying snack combining fruit, fiber, and healthy fats.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Apple (medium)\",\"amount\":\"1 unit\",\"calories\":95},{\"name\":\"Peanut Butter (natural)\",\"amount\":\"2 tbsp (32g)\",\"calories\":190}],\"totalCalories\":285,\"macros\":{\"protein\":8,\"carbs\":26,\"fat\":16},\"instructions\":[\"Slice the apple into wedges.\",\"Spread peanut butter on apple slices and enjoy.\"]}},\"dailyTotals\":{\"calories\":1762,\"protein\":101,\"carbs\":186,\"fat\":74}},{\"dayNumber\":4,\"date\":\"Day 4\",\"meals\":{\"breakfast\":{\"name\":\"Vietnamese Savory Oatmeal (Cháo Yến Mạch Mặn)\",\"time\":\"7:00 AM\",\"description\":\"A hearty and flavorful Vietnamese twist on oatmeal, packed with protein.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Rolled Oats (dry)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":190},{\"name\":\"Lean Ground Pork/Chicken\",\"amount\":\"80g\",\"calories\":120},{\"name\":\"Chicken Broth (low sodium)\",\"amount\":\"250ml\",\"calories\":15},{\"name\":\"Mushrooms (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Green Onions (chopped)\",\"amount\":\"10g\",\"calories\":3},{\"name\":\"Ginger (grated)\",\"amount\":\"5g\",\"calories\":5},{\"name\":\"Fish Sauce (light)\",\"amount\":\"5ml\",\"calories\":3}],\"totalCalories\":346,\"macros\":{\"protein\":24,\"carbs\":40,\"fat\":9},\"instructions\":[\"In a saucepan, combine oats and chicken broth. Bring to a simmer and cook until oats are tender, stirring occasionally.\",\"In a separate small pan, cook ground pork/chicken with a dash of fish sauce, grated ginger, and a pinch of pepper until browned.\",\"Add cooked meat and sliced mushrooms to the oatmeal. Cook for another 2-3 minutes.\",\"Garnish with chopped green onions before serving.\"]},\"lunch\":{\"name\":\"Tuna Salad Lettuce Wraps with Whole-Wheat Crackers\",\"time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A light, high-protein lunch with crunchy textures.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Canned Tuna (in water, drained)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":165},{\"name\":\"Greek Yogurt (plain, non-fat)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Celery (chopped)\",\"amount\":\"30g\",\"calories\":5},{\"name\":\"Red Onion (finely diced)\",\"amount\":\"10g\",\"calories\":4},{\"name\":\"Lemon Juice\",\"amount\":\"5ml\",\"calories\":2},{\"name\":\"Large Lettuce Leaves (e.g., butter lettuce)\",\"amount\":\"4 leaves\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Whole-Wheat Crackers\",\"amount\":\"30g (approx. 5-6 crackers)\",\"calories\":130}],\"totalCalories\":346,\"macros\":{\"protein\":35,\"carbs\":30,\"fat\":9},\"instructions\":[\"In a bowl, flake the drained tuna. Add Greek yogurt, chopped celery, diced red onion, lemon juice, salt, and pepper. Mix well.\",\"Spoon the tuna salad into large lettuce leaves to create wraps.\",\"Serve with whole-wheat crackers on the side.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Chicken & Veggie Skewers with Quinoa\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"Colorful and lean skewers served with a protein-rich grain.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Chicken Breast (cubed)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":240},{\"name\":\"Quinoa (cooked)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":180},{\"name\":\"Bell Peppers (cubed, mixed colors)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":30},{\"name\":\"Zucchini (cubed)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":20},{\"name\":\"Cherry Tomatoes\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":9},{\"name\":\"Olive Oil (for marinade/grilling)\",\"amount\":\"10ml\",\"calories\":90},{\"name\":\"Herbs & Spices (paprika, garlic powder)\",\"amount\":\"to taste\",\"calories\":5}],\"totalCalories\":574,\"macros\":{\"protein\":39,\"carbs\":50,\"fat\":24},\"instructions\":[\"If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for 30 minutes.\",\"Toss cubed chicken and vegetables with olive oil, herbs, spices, salt, and pepper.\",\"Thread chicken and vegetables alternately onto 