the side or on toast.\"]},\"lunch\":{\"name\":\"Leftover Chicken & Veggie Skewers with Quinoa\",\"time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"description\":\"Enjoy the delicious leftovers from last night\'s dinner for a convenient and balanced lunch.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Chicken & Veggie Skewers\",\"amount\":\"Portion from Day 4 dinner\",\"calories\":300},{\"name\":\"Quinoa (cooked)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":120}],\"totalCalories\":420,\"macros\":{\"protein\":30,\"carbs\":40,\"fat\":15},\"instructions\":[\"Reheat leftover chicken and veggie skewers in a microwave or oven until warmed through.\",\"Serve with the remaining cooked quinoa from yesterday, or cook a fresh batch if needed.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Vietnamese Pork & Egg Meatloaf (Chả Trứng Hấp) with Brown Rice & Pickled Veggies\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"A healthier take on the classic Cơm Tấm side dish, served with broken brown rice and vibrant pickled vegetables.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Lean Ground Pork\",\"amount\":\"120g\",\"calories\":200},{\"name\":\"Eggs\",\"amount\":\"2 units\",\"calories\":140},{\"name\":\"Glass Noodles (uncooked)\",\"amount\":\"15g\",\"calories\":50},{\"name\":\"Wood Ear Mushrooms (dried, rehydrated)\",\"amount\":\"5g\",\"calories\":10},{\"name\":\"Shallots (minced)\",\"amount\":\"10g\",\"calories\":5},{\"name\":\"Brown Rice (cooked, \'broken rice\' style)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":165},{\"name\":\"Pickled Carrots & Daikon (Do Chua)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":15},{\"name\":\"Fish Sauce (light, for dipping)\",\"amount\":\"10ml\",\"calories\":5}],\"totalCalories\":590,\"macros\":{\"protein\":35,\"carbs\":60,\"fat\":20},\"instructions\":[\"Rehydrate glass noodles and wood ear mushrooms, then chop finely.\",\"In a bowl, combine ground pork, 1 whole egg, glass noodles, wood ear mushrooms, minced shallots, a pinch of fish sauce, salt, and pepper. Mix well.\",\"Press mixture into a small heatproof dish. Whisk the remaining egg and pour evenly over the top.\",\"Steam for 20-25 minutes, or until cooked through and egg topping is set.\",\"Cook brown rice. Prepare Do Chua (pickled carrots and daikon) if not pre-made.\",\"Slice the steamed pork and egg meatloaf. Serve with brown rice, pickled vegetables, and a light fish sauce dipping sauce.\"]},\"snack\":{\"name\":\"Rice Cakes with Hummus & Cucumber\",\"time\":\"3:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A light and crunchy snack with plant-based protein and fiber.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Plain Rice Cakes\",\"amount\":\"2 units\",\"calories\":70},{\"name\":\"Hummus\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":80},{\"name\":\"Cucumber (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":8}],\"totalCalories\":158,\"macros\":{\"protein\":5,\"carbs\":25,\"fat\":5},\"instructions\":[\"Spread hummus evenly over rice cakes.\",\"Top with sliced cucumber. Enjoy.\"]}},\"dailyTotals\":{\"calories\":1612,\"protein\":91,\"carbs\":163,\"fat\":60}},{\"dayNumber\":6,\"date\":\"Day 6\",\"meals\":{\"breakfast\":{\"name\":\"Greek Yogurt Parfait with Granola & Fruit\",\"time\":\"7:00 AM\",\"description\":\"A layered breakfast offering protein, fiber, and natural sweetness.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Greek Yogurt (plain, non-fat)\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":90},{\"name\":\"Granola (low sugar)\",\"amount\":\"40g\",\"calories\":180},{\"name\":\"Mixed Berries (fresh)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":50},{\"name\":\"Honey (optional, small drizzle)\",\"amount\":\"5g\",\"calories\":15}],\"totalCalories\":335,\"macros\":{\"protein\":18,\"carbs\":50,\"fat\":7},\"instructions\":[\"In a glass or bowl, layer Greek yogurt, granola, and mixed berries.\",\"Repeat layers if desired. Drizzle with a small amount of honey if extra sweetness is preferred. Serve immediately.\"]},\"lunch\":{\"name\":\"Chicken and Vegetable Noodle Soup (Phở Gà style, lighter)\",\"time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A comforting and nourishing Vietnamese-inspired soup, lighter on broth and oil.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Chicken Breast (shredded, cooked)\",\"amount\":\"120g\",\"calories\":192},{\"name\":\"Rice Noodles (Phở style, cooked)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":130},{\"name\":\"Chicken Broth (low sodium)\",\"amount\":\"300ml\",\"calories\":20},{\"name\":\"Bean Sprouts\",\"amount\":\"50g\",\"calories\":8},{\"name\":\"Green Onions (chopped)\",\"amount\":\"10g\",\"calories\":3},{\"name\":\"Cilantro (chopped)\",\"amount\":\"10g\",\"calories\":3},{\"name\":\"Lime Wedge\",\"amount\":\"1 unit\",\"calories\":2},{\"name\":\"Optional: Chili Slices\",\"amount\":\"to taste\",\"calories\":1}],\"totalCalories\":359,\"macros\":{\"protein\":34,\"carbs\":44,\"fat\":5},\"instructions\":[\"Bring low-sodium chicken broth to a simmer. Add shredded cooked chicken breast and heat through.\",\"Cook rice noodles according to package instructions.\",\"In a large bowl, place cooked rice noodles. Pour hot broth and chicken over the noodles.\",\"Top with fresh bean sprouts, chopped green onions, and cilantro. Serve with a lime wedge and chili slices if desired.\"]},\"dinner\":{\"name\":\"Baked Cod with Roasted Root Vegetables\",\"time\":\"7:00 PM\",\"description\":\"A simple and clean dinner featuring flaky white fish and wholesome roasted vegetables.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Cod Fillet\",\"amount\":\"150g\",\"calories\":120},{\"name\":\"Potatoes (small, diced)\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":80},{\"name\":\"Carrots (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"80g\",\"calories\":32},{\"name\":\"Parsnips (sliced)\",\"amount\":\"80g\",\"calories\":60},{\"name\":\"Broccoli Florets\",\"amount\":\"100g\",\"calories\":35},{\"name\":\"Olive Oil\",\"amount\":\"10ml\",\"calories\":90},{\"name\":\"Lemon Slices\",\"amount\":\"2 units\",\"calories\":4},{\"name\":\"Dill (fresh, chopped)\",\"amount\":\"5g\",\"calories\":1}],\"totalCalories\":422,\"macros\":{\"protein\":27,\"carbs\":50,\"fat\":15},\"instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 200°C (400°F).\",\"Toss diced potatoes, carrots, and parsnips with 5ml olive oil, salt, and pepper. Spread on a baking sheet and roast for 20 minutes.\",\"Add broccoli to the baking sheet and roast for another 10 minutes.\",\"Season cod fillet with salt, pepper, and fresh dill. Place on a separate baking sheet or parchment paper with lemon slices on top. Drizzle with remaining 5ml olive oil.\",\"Bake cod for 12-15 minutes, or until it flakes easily with a fork.\",\"Serve baked cod with roasted root vegetables and broccoli.\"]},\"snack\":{\"name\":\"Hard-Boiled Eggs & Orange\",\"time\":\"3:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A simple, protein-rich snack paired with a refreshing citrus fruit.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Hard-Boiled Eggs (large)\",\"amount\":\"2 units\",\"calories\":140},{\"name\":\"Orange (medium)\",\"amount\":\"1 unit\",\"calories\":70}],\"totalCalories\":210,\"macros\":{\"protein\":12,\"carbs\":18,\"fat\":10},\"instructions\":[\"Peel hard-boiled eggs. Peel and segment the orange.\",\"Enjoy together as a quick snack.\"]}},\"dailyTotals\":{\"calories\":1326,\"protein\":91,\"carbs\":162,\"fat\":37}},{\"dayNumber\":7,\"date\":\"Day 7\",\"meals\":{\"breakfast\":{\"name\":\"Cereal with Protein Milk & Berries\",\"time\":\"7:00 AM\",\"description\":\"A quick and easy breakfast with a protein boost.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Whole-Grain Cereal (low sugar)\",\"amount\":\"40g\",\"calories\":150},{\"name\":\"Skim Milk\",\"amount\":\"200ml\",\"calories\":70},{\"name\":\"Whey Protein Powder (unflavored/vanilla)\",\"amount\":\"15g\",\"calories\":60},{\"name\":\"Mixed Berries (fresh)\",\"amount\":\"80g\",\"calories\":40}],\"totalCalories\":320,\"macros\":{\"protein\":23,\"carbs\":45,\"fat\":3},\"instructions\":[\"Pour cereal into a bowl.\",\"Mix protein powder into skim milk until fully dissolved. Pour over cereal.\",\"Top with fresh mixed berries and serve.\"]},\"lunch\":{\"name\":\"Shrimp & Avocado Salad with Whole-Wheat Pita\",\"time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"description\":\"A light yet satisfying salad with lean protein, healthy fats, and whole grains.\",\"foods\":[{\"name\":\"Cooked Shrimp\",\"amount\":\"120g\",\"calories\":1