INSERT INTO `workout_plans` VALUES (2,2,'Beginner\'s 4-Week Full Body Fitness Program','A comprehensive 4-week program designed for a 21-year-old male beginner to build foundational strength, improve cardiovascular health, and enhance overall general fitness. This plan focuses on progressive overload, varied exercises, and adequate recovery to ensure steady progress.','general_fitness',4,4,'beginner','{\"weeklyStructure\":\"Each week includes two full-body strength workouts, two cardio-focused sessions (one with core, one with active recovery/flexibility), and three dedicated rest days. This structure allows for muscle recovery and skill development while building endurance.\",\"progressionNotes\":\"Increase sets, reps, or duration progressively each week. For strength exercises, aim to increase reps by 1-2 or move to 4 sets in later weeks. For cardio, increase duration by 5 minutes or introduce short bursts of higher intensity. Always prioritize proper form over intensity, especially as a beginner. If a set number of reps is listed but you can\'t complete it with good form, do as many as you can and aim for more next time.\",\"tips\":[\"Listen to your body: If you feel pain, stop the exercise and rest. Modify as needed.\",\"Stay hydrated: Drink plenty of water throughout the day, especially around your workouts.\",\"Nutrition matters: Support your workouts with a balanced diet rich in protein, complex carbohydrates, and healthy fats.\",\"Consistency is key: Stick to your schedule as much as possible for best results.\",\"Prioritize sleep: Aim for 7-9 hours of quality sleep to aid in recovery and muscle repair.\",\"Focus on form: As a beginner, mastering the correct form for each exercise is more important than lifting heavy or going fast.\"]}',1,'2025-11-25 13:32:18','2025-12-23 13:32:18','{\"0\":\"{\",\"1\":\"\\\"\",\"2\":\"c\",\"3\":\"o\",\"4\":\"m\",\"5\":\"p\",\"6\":\"l\",\"7\":\"e\",\"8\":\"t\",\"9\":\"e\",\"10\":\"d\",\"11\":\"W\",\"12\":\"o\",\"13\":\"r\",\"14\":\"k\",\"15\":\"o\",\"16\":\"u\",\"17\":\"t\",\"18\":\"s\",\"19\":\"\\\"\",\"20\":\":\",\"21\":\"0\",\"22\":\",\",\"23\":\"\\\"\",\"24\":\"t\",\"25\":\"o\",\"26\":\"t\",\"27\":\"a\",\"28\":\"l\",\"29\":\"W\",\"30\":\"o\",\"31\":\"r\",\"32\":\"k\",\"33\":\"o\",\"34\":\"u\",\"35\":\"t\",\"36\":\"s\",\"37\":\"\\\"\",\"38\":\":\",\"39\":\"1\",\"40\":\"6\",\"41\":\",\",\"42\":\"\\\"\",\"43\":\"a\",\"44\":\"v\",\"45\":\"e\",\"46\":\"r\",\"47\":\"a\",\"48\":\"g\",\"49\":\"e\",\"50\":\"R\",\"51\":\"a\",\"52\":\"t\",\"53\":\"i\",\"54\":\"n\",\"55\":\"g\",\"56\":\"\\\"\",\"57\":\":\",\"58\":\"0\",\"59\":\"}\",\"completedWorkouts\":1,\"totalWorkouts\":16}',1,'Goal: general_fitness, Duration: 4 weeks, Frequency: 4/week','2025-11-25 13:32:18','2025-11-25 13:39:51'),(3,2,'Beginner 4-Week Full Body Fitness Journey','This 4-week program is designed for a 21-year-old male beginner with general fitness goals. It integrates full-body strength training, cardiovascular endurance, and mobility work to build a strong foundation, improve stamina, and enhance overall physical well-being. The plan progresses gradually to ensure safe and effective development, focusing on form and consistency.','general_fitness',4,4,'beginner','{\"weeklyStructure\":\"The weekly schedule is structured around 4 workout days and 3 dedicated rest days. Workouts typically alternate between full-body strength and a combination of cardio & core/mobility. This consistent pattern ensures balanced muscle development, cardiovascular improvement, and adequate recovery for a beginner.\",\"progressionNotes\":\"The plan systematically increases intensity over the 4 weeks. Progression is achieved by gradually: \\n1. Increasing the number of repetitions for strength exercises.\\n2. Extending the duration for cardio exercises and plank holds.\\n3. Reducing rest periods between sets/exercises (where appropriate) to enhance endurance.\\n4. Introducing more sets for some exercises in later weeks.\\nAlways prioritize maintaining proper form, even if it means not hitting the exact prescribed numbers. Listen to your body and adjust if necessary, ensuring a sustainable and injury-free progression.\",\"tips\":[\"Focus on proper form: Quality over quantity. Mastering the movement pattern is key to preventing injury and maximizing results.\",\"Stay hydrated: Drink plenty of water throughout the day, especially before, during, and after workouts, to support performance and recovery.\",\"Listen to your body: It\'s okay to modify exercises, take extra rest, or reduce intensity if you feel pain or excessive fatigue. Consistency is more important than pushing too hard too soon.\",\"Prioritize recovery: Aim for 7-9 hours of quality sleep each night. Sleep is when your muscles repair and grow, and your body recovers.\",\"Nutrition matters: Fuel your body with a balanced diet rich in whole foods, lean proteins, complex carbohydrates, and healthy fats to support your training, energy levels, and overall health.\",\"Track your progress: Keep a simple log of your workouts. Seeing your improvements can be a great motivator and help you adjust the plan.\"]}',1,'2025-11-25 15:44:23','2025-12-23 15:44:23','{\"completedWorkouts\":0,\"totalWorkouts\":16,\"averageRating\":0}',1,'Goal: general_fitness, Duration: 4 weeks, Frequency: 4/week','2025-11-25 15:44:23','2025-11-25 15:44:23'),(4,3,'Beginner\'s 4-Week Full-Body Fitness Journey','A progressive 4-week workout plan designed for a 21-year-old female beginner, focusing on general fitness. This plan combines strength, cardio, and flexibility, with workouts adaptable for both home and gym environments. It emphasizes building a strong foundation and gradually increasing intensity.','general_fitness',4,4,'beginner','{\"weeklyStructure\":\"The plan follows a 4-day workout split per week: two full-body strength sessions (one home-focused, one gym/adaptable), and two cardio sessions (one with core focus, one with flexibility). Rest days are strategically placed to ensure adequate recovery and promote muscle growth.\",\"progressionNotes\":\"Progression is built into the plan by gradually increasing reps, sets, duration, and intensity over the four weeks. \\n- **Weeks 1-2:** Focus on mastering form and building foundational strength and endurance.\\n- **Weeks 3-4:** Increase volume (more sets/reps/duration) and intensity (shorter rest, introduction of sprint intervals, slight increase in weights if at gym). You are encouraged to challenge yourself safely.\",\"tips\":[\"**Listen to Your Body:** This plan is a guide. If you feel pain, stop the exercise. Modify or rest as needed. Don\'t push through discomfort.\",\"**Focus on Form:** Especially as a beginner, prioritize correct form over lifting heavy or doing more reps. Watch instructional videos for exercises if unsure.\",\"**Stay Hydrated:** Drink plenty of water throughout the day, especially before, during, and after workouts.\",\"**Nutrition is Key:** Support your workouts with a balanced diet rich in whole foods, lean protein, healthy fats, and complex carbohydrates.\",\"**Consistency Over Perfection:** Aim for consistency. Missing a day isn\'t a failure, just get back on track with your next scheduled workout.\",\"**Warm-up & Cool-down:** Never skip these! They prepare your body for exercise and aid in recovery, reducing injury risk.\",\"**Utilize Your Environment:** For \'adaptable\' strength days, use dumbbells, resistance bands, or even household items (like full water bottles) if you\'re at home, or gym equipment if you\'re at the gym.\"],\"workoutLocation\":\"Both gym and home\"}',1,'2025-11-25 16:59:41','2025-12-23 16:59:41','{\"completedWorkouts\":0,\"totalWorkouts\":16,\"averageRating\":0}',1,'Goal: general_fitness, Duration: 4 weeks, Frequency: 4/week, Location: Both gym and home','2025-11-25 16:59:41','2025-11-25 16:59:41'),(5,4,'Beginner\'s Balanced Foundation - 4-Week Program','A comprehensive 4-week workout plan designed for a 21-year-old female beginner, focusing on general fitness. This plan combines full-body strength training (at home and gym) with cardio and flexibility sessions, all strictly within a 60-minute time limit per session, 4 times per week.','general_fitness',4,4,'beginner','{\"weeklyStructure\":\"The weekly structure consists of 4 workout days and 3 rest days. Workouts alternate between full-body strength sessions at the gym and at home, with one day specifically dedicated to cardio, core, and flexibility at home. This balanced approach ensures comprehensive fitness development.\",\"progressionNotes\":\"The plan progresses by gradually increasing the number of repetitions, sets, and workout duration over the 4 weeks. For strength exercises, you\'ll move from 3 sets of 10-12 reps to 3-4 sets of 12-15 reps, potentially incorporating more challenging variations (e.g., full push-ups). Cardio duration will incrementally increase, and core holds will extend. Listen to your body and only increase intensity when proper form can be maintained.\",\"tips\":[\"**Prioritize Form:** As a beginner, perfect form is more important than lifting heavy or doing many reps. Watch videos, use mirrors, and don\'t hesitate to reduce intensity to maintain proper technique.\",\"**Listen to Your Body:** Rest days are crucial for muscle recovery and growth. If you feel excessive soreness or fatigue, take an extra rest day or modify your workout.\",\"**Stay Hydrated:** Drink plenty of water throughout the day, especially before, during, and after workouts.\",\"**Nutrition is Key:** Fuel your body with balanced meals that include lean protein, complex carbohydrates, and healthy fats to support your training and recovery.\",\"**Warm-up & Cool-down:** Always perform the recommended warm-up before your workout to prepare your muscles and cool-down stretches afterward to improve flexibility and aid recovery.\",\"**Consistency Over Perfection:** Missing a workout isn\'t a failure, it\'s an opportunity to get back on track. Consistency is the most important factor for long-term progress.\",\"**Journal Your Progress:** Keeping a log of your sets, reps, and how you felt can help you track your improvements and stay motivated.\"],\"workoutLocation\":\"Both gym and home\"}',0,'2025-11-25 17:31:48','2025-12-23 17:31:48','{\"completedWorkouts\":0,\"totalWorkouts\":16,\"averageRating\":0}',1,'Goal: general_fitness, Duration: 4 weeks, Frequency: 4/week, Location: Both gym and home','2025-11-25 17:31:48','2025-11-25 17:31:48');
INSERT INTO `workout_plans` VALUES (7,4,'Beginner\'s Journey: 4-Week General Fitness Plan','A personalized 4-week workout program designed for a 21-year-old female beginner, focusing on building general fitness through a balanced mix of strength, cardio, and flexibility. The plan incorporates both home and gym workouts, with a clear progression in intensity while strictly adhering to a 60-minute maximum session duration.','general_fitness',4,4,'beginner','{\"weeklyStructure\":\"Each week consists of 4 workout days and 3 rest days. Workouts are split into three full-body strength and cardio sessions (alternating between home and gym focus), and one dedicated cardio and flexibility session (home/outdoor). This structure ensures balanced development across major muscle groups and cardiovascular endurance, while allowing ample recovery.\",\"progressionNotes\":\"The plan follows a progressive overload principle over the 4 weeks. \\n- **Strength Exercises:** Weeks 1-2 focus on establishing proper form with 3 sets of 8-12 reps (or specified duration). Weeks 3-4 increase to 3-4 sets of 10-15 reps or longer hold times (e.g., plank), encouraging a slight increase in intensity or bodyweight challenge. For gym-based exercises, a gradual increase in weight is encouraged if form is maintained.\\n- **Cardio Exercises:** Duration for cardio sessions gradually increases from 15-16 minutes in Weeks 1-2 to 20-22 minutes in Weeks 3-4. New cardio exercises are introduced for variety and to challenge different muscle groups and energy systems.\\n- **Flexibility Exercises:** Hold times for stretches increase from 30 seconds to 45 seconds in later weeks.\\n- **Listen to Your Body:** Always prioritize proper form over speed or number of reps/duration. If an exercise feels too difficult, modify it (e.g., knee push-ups). If it feels too easy, increase reps, sets, or duration as suggested for progression.\",\"tips\":[\"**Consistency is Key:** Stick to your schedule as much as possible. If you miss a day, pick it up the next day rather than skipping the workout entirely.\",\"**Hydration and Nutrition:** Drink plenty of water throughout the day, especially around your workouts. Fuel your body with balanced meals rich in protein, complex carbohydrates, and healthy fats to support recovery and energy levels.\",\"**Listen to Your Body:** Pay attention to how your body feels. Some soreness is normal, but sharp pain is not. Don\'t be afraid to take an extra rest day or modify exercises if needed.\",\"**Warm-up and Cool-down:** Never skip these! They prepare your body for exercise, prevent injury, and aid in recovery.\",\"**Focus on Form:** Especially as a beginner, mastering the correct form for each exercise is more important than lifting heavy or doing many reps. Watch videos, use mirrors, or consult a trainer if unsure.\",\"**Mind-Muscle Connection:** Try to actively feel the muscles working during each exercise. This enhances effectiveness and prevents other muscles from taking over.\",\"**Sleep:** Aim for 7-9 hours of quality sleep per night. It\'s crucial for muscle repair, hormone regulation, and overall well-being.\"],\"workoutLocation\":\"Both gym and home\"}',0,'2025-11-25 18:20:06','2025-12-23 18:20:06','{\"0\":\"{\",\"1\":\"\\\"\",\"2\":\"0\",\"3\":\"\\\"\",\"4\":\":\",\"5\":\"\\\"\",\"6\":\"{\",\"7\":\"\\\"\",\"8\":\",\",\"9\":\"\\\"\",\"10\":\"1\",\"11\":\"\\\"\",\"12\":\":\",\"13\":\"\\\"\",\"14\":\"\\\\\",\"15\":\"\\\"\",\"16\":\"\\\"\",\"17\":\",\",\"18\":\"\\\"\",\"19\":\"2\",\"20\":\"\\\"\",\"21\":\":\",\"22\":\"\\\"\",\"23\":\"0\",\"24\":\"\\\"\",\"25\":\",\",\"26\":\"\\\"\",\"27\":\"3\",\"28\":\"\\\"\",\"29\":\":\",\"30\":\"\\\"\",\"31\":\"\\\\\",\"32\":\"\\\"\",\"33\":\"\\\"\",\"34\":\",\",\"35\":\"\\\"\",\"36\":\"4\",\"37\":\"\\\"\",\"38\":\":\",\"39\":\"\\\"\",\"40\":\":\",\"41\":\"\\\"\",\"42\":\",\",\"43\":\"\\\"\",\"44\":\"5\",\"45\":\"\\\"\",\"46\":\":\",\"47\":\"\\\"\",\"48\":\"\\\\\",\"49\":\"\\\"\",\"50\":\"\\\"\",\"51\":\",\",\"5